---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Open Source — Tracepod"
  description="Tracepod's eBPF sensor, hardener, CLI, Helm chart, and GitHub Action are fully open source under AGPL-3.0. Install in minutes."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="oss-hero section">
    <div class="container oss-hero-inner">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Open Source &middot; AGPL-3.0</div>
        <h1 class="heading-xl">The full hardening toolchain, free and open.</h1>
        <p class="body-lg" style="margin-top: 1.5rem; max-width: 600px;">
          The eBPF sensor, image builder, CLI, Helm chart, and GitHub Action are all
          open source. Everything you need to start hardening containers today, with
          no lock-in and no telemetry.
        </p>
        <div style="display:flex; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 2rem; flex-wrap: wrap;">
          <a href="https://github.com/tracepod/tracepod" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-primary">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 2C6.477 2 2 6.484 2 12.017c0 4.425 2.865 8.18 6.839 9.504.5.092.682-.217.682-.483 0-.237-.008-.868-.013-1.703-2.782.605-3.369-1.343-3.369-1.343-.454-1.158-1.11-1.466-1.11-1.466-.908-.62.069-.608.069-.608 1.003.07 1.531 1.032 1.531 1.032.892 1.53 2.341 1.088 2.91.832.092-.647.35-1.088.636-1.338-2.22-.253-4.555-1.113-4.555-4.951 0-1.093.39-1.988 1.029-2.688-.103-.253-.446-1.272.098-2.65 0 0 .84-.27 2.75 1.026A9.564 9.564 0 0112 6.844c.85.004 1.705.115 2.504.337 1.909-1.296 2.747-1.027 2.747-1.027.546 1.379.202 2.398.1 2.651.64.7 1.028 1.595 1.028 2.688 0 3.848-2.339 4.695-4.566 4.943.359.309.678.92.678 1.855 0 1.338-.012 2.419-.012 2.747 0 .268.18.58.688.482A10.019 10.019 0 0022 12.017C22 6.484 17.522 2 12 2z"/></svg>
            View on GitHub
          </a>
          <a href="/docs" class="btn btn-secondary">Read the docs</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Tools grid -->
  <section class="section--tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="text-align:center; margin-bottom: 3rem;">What's included</div>
      <div class="tools-grid">

        <div class="tool-card card">
          <div class="tool-icon">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/>
              <path d="M12 1v4M12 19v4M4.22 4.22l2.83 2.83M16.95 16.95l2.83 2.83M1 12h4M19 12h4M4.22 19.78l2.83-2.83M16.95 7.05l2.83-2.83"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3>eBPF Sensor</h3>
          <p>
            CO-RE kprobe sensor written in pure Go using <code>cilium/ebpf</code>.
            Attaches to <code>openat()</code>, filters by cgroup/namespace, ships events over a ring buffer.
            Runs as a DaemonSet pod. No kernel module, no DKMS, no side-cars.
          </p>
          <div class="tool-tags">
            <span class="tag">Go 1.26</span>
            <span class="tag">cilium/ebpf</span>
            <span class="tag">CO-RE</span>
            <span class="tag">kernel 6.8+</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tool-card card">
          <div class="tool-icon">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
              <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/>
              <path d="M9 9h6M9 12h6M9 15h4"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Image Builder (hardener)</h3>
          <p>
            Takes the sensor manifest, resolves ELF shared-library dependencies recursively
            via readelf + ld.so.conf, applies language-runtime companion rules, then emits a
            new OCI image layer containing only the files that were actually observed.
          </p>
          <div class="tool-tags">
            <span class="tag">go-containerregistry</span>
            <span class="tag">ELF resolver</span>
            <span class="tag">CGO-free</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tool-card card">
          <div class="tool-icon">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
              <polyline points="4 17 10 11 4 5"/>
              <line x1="12" y1="19" x2="20" y2="19"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3>CLI (<code>tracepod</code> + <code>harden</code>)</h3>
          <p>
            Two static binaries. <code>tracepod</code> talks to the in-cluster controller:
            <code>profile list</code>, <code>profile get</code>, <code>profile stop</code>, <code>cve-report</code>.
            <code>harden</code> builds and pushes the minimised image from a profile. Both CGO-free,
            built for linux and darwin on amd64 and arm64.
          </p>
          <div class="tool-tags">
            <span class="tag">Static binary</span>
            <span class="tag">linux/amd64</span>
            <span class="tag">linux/arm64</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tool-card card">
          <div class="tool-icon">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M21 16V8a2 2 0 0 0-1-1.73l-7-4a2 2 0 0 0-2 0l-7 4A2 2 0 0 0 3 8v8a2 2 0 0 0 1 1.73l7 4a2 2 0 0 0 2 0l7-4A2 2 0 0 0 21 16z"/>
              <polyline points="3.27 6.96 12 12.01 20.73 6.96"/>
              <line x1="12" y1="22.08" x2="12" y2="12"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Helm Chart</h3>
          <p>
            Official Helm chart for Kubernetes deployment: DaemonSet for the sensor,
            aggregation controller deployment, RBAC (ClusterRole + ServiceAccount),
            ConfigMap-based role definitions. Exercised end-to-end on kind in CI.
          </p>
          <div class="tool-tags">
            <span class="tag">Helm 3</span>
            <span class="tag">DaemonSet</span>
            <span class="tag">RBAC</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tool-card card">
          <div class="tool-icon">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
              <polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3>GitHub Action</h3>
          <p>
            Add a <code>uses: tracepod/tracepod@v0</code> step to your release workflow.
            Give it a recorded profile and a source image; it builds, smoke-tests, and
            SBOMs the hardened image, and can push it alongside the original.
          </p>
          <div class="tool-tags">
            <span class="tag">GitHub Actions</span>
            <span class="tag">SBOM output</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tool-card card">
          <div class="tool-icon">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/>
              <polyline points="9 12 11 14 15 10"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Seccomp + AppArmor + SBOMs</h3>
          <p>
            Syscall allowlist (seccomp JSON) and AppArmor profile generated from the observed
            syscall set. CycloneDX and SPDX SBOMs produced by syft and signed with cosign.
            Both attestation formats pushed alongside the image.
          </p>
          <div class="tool-tags">
            <span class="tag">seccomp</span>
            <span class="tag">AppArmor</span>
            <span class="tag">CycloneDX</span>
            <span class="tag">SPDX</span>
            <span class="tag">cosign</span>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Install snippet -->
  <section class="install-section section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="install-inner">
        <div class="install-text">
          <div class="eyebrow">Installation</div>
          <h2 class="heading-lg">Up and running in under five minutes.</h2>
          <p class="body-md" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
            Install the sensor with the Helm chart from the repo, and grab the CLI
            binaries from GitHub releases. The sensor needs nodes running kernel 6.8
            or newer with containerd NRI enabled.
          </p>
          <a href="/docs/getting-started/installation/" class="btn btn-secondary" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
            Full installation guide &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="install-terminal terminal">
          <div class="terminal-bar">
            <div class="terminal-dot"></div>
            <div class="terminal-dot"></div>
            <div class="terminal-dot"></div>
            <span class="terminal-title">Install Tracepod</span>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal-body">
            <p><span class="comment"># Kubernetes: sensor + controller via the Helm chart</span></p>
            <p><span class="prompt">$</span> git clone https://github.com/tracepod/tracepod</p>
            <p><span class="prompt">$</span> helm install tracepod ./tracepod/helm/tracepod \</p>
            <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;--namespace tracepod --create-namespace</p>
            <p>&nbsp;</p>
            <p><span class="comment"># CLI binaries from GitHub releases</span></p>
            <p><span class="prompt">$</span> curl -fsSLO https://github.com/tracepod/tracepod/releases/download/\</p>
            <p>v0.1.2/tracepod_tracepod_0.1.2_linux_amd64.tar.gz</p>
            <p><span class="prompt">$</span> tar xzf tracepod_tracepod_0.1.2_linux_amd64.tar.gz -C /usr/local/bin</p>
            <p>&nbsp;</p>
            <p><span class="comment"># Verify</span></p>
            <p><span class="prompt">$</span> tracepod version</p>
            <p><span class="success">tracepod v0.1.2 (2f8a41c)</span></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="cta-band section">
    <div class="container cta-band-inner">
      <div>
        <h2 class="heading-lg">Want the full platform?</h2>
        <p class="body-md" style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
          The Tracepod platform adds a web dashboard, sandbox validation, auto-fix, CVE delta reports, and more.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-shrink: 0;">
        <a href="/platform" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg">See the platform</a>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Contact us</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
.oss-hero { padding-top: var(--space-16); }
.oss-hero-inner { max-width: 800px; }

.tools-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  gap: var(--space-6);
}

.tool-card {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--space-3);
}

.tool-icon {
  width: 44px;
  height: 44px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--accent-dim);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  color: var(--accent);
  flex-shrink: 0;
}

.tool-card h3 { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; }
.tool-card p { font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; }
.tool-card code { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.85em; }

.tool-tags {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: var(--space-2);
  margin-top: auto;
}
.tag {
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 0.7rem;
  padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
}

.install-inner {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr;
  gap: var(--space-12);
  align-items: start;
}
.install-text { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-4); }

.cta-band { background: var(--bg-elevated); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
.cta-band-inner { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--space-8); }
.btn-lg { padding: 0.8rem 1.75rem; font-size: 1rem; }

@media (max-width: 960px) {
  .tools-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  .install-inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}
@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .tools-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .cta-band-inner { flex-direction: column; text-align: center; }
}
</style>
